    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="24">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 24</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ nan man nan þingc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.7"/> ne bigce ofer feower peniwurð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.8"/>, ne libbende ne licgende, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.1"/> man hæbbe getrywe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.9"/> gewitnesse feower manna, seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.10-2"/> hit binnan byrig, sy hit upp<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.11-2"/> on lande.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ nan man nan ðing ne bycge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.4"/> ofer feower peninga weorð, ne libbende ne licgende, buton mon habbe getreowe gewitnysse feower manna, sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.5"/> hit binnan byrig, sy hit up<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.6"/> on lande.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>And nan man nan þincg ne bycge ofer feower penigweorð, ne libbende ne licgende, buton man hæbbe getreowe gewitnesse feower manna, sy hit binnan byrig, sy hit up on lande.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Et nemo aliquid emat supra IIII denariorum ualens, mobile uel inmobile<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.star"/>, nisi habeat credibile testimonium IIII hominum, sit in ciuitate, sit extra.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.10"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Uolumus etiam, ut nullus emat aliquid ultra quattuor denariorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.8-2"/> ualens, nec rem uiuam nec<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.9-2"/> mortuam nec iacentem, sine quattuor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_24.lnote.oe.10-3"/> idoneis testibus, nec infra burgum nec extra.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Et nemo emat quicquam supra ualorem IIII denariorum, tam uiuum quam mortuum, nisi habeat fidele testimonium IIII hominum, siue urbi siue ruri.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="24" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="186" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ nan man nan ðing ne bycge ofer feower peninga weorð, ne libbende ne licgende, buton mon habbe getreowe gewitnysse feower manna, sy hit binnan byrig, sy hit up<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_24.robnote.fn.4"/> on lande.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="266" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And nan man nan þingc ne bigce ofer feower peniwurð, ne libbende ne licgende, butan man hæbbe getrywe gewitnesse feower manna, seo hit binnan byrig, sy hit upp on lande.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24.lnote.de.1"/> niemand kaufe etwas über 4<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_24.lnote.de.2"/> Pfennigwerth (-ge Werth <hi rend="italic">B</hi>), weder lebendes noch liegendes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#IICn_24.lnote.de1.dagger"/>, ohne dass er Zeugenschaft von 4<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_24.lnote.de.2"/> glaubwürdigen Männern hat, sei das [Kaufen] in der Stadt oder auf dem Lande.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let no one buy anything over four pennies' worth, either living or lying [dead chattels], unless he has the trustworthy witness of four men, whether it be in a borough or up in the country.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="187" ed="#robertson"/>And no-one shall buy anything over four pence in value, either livestock or other property<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24.robnote.n.1"/>, unless he have four men as trustworthy witnesses, whether [the purchase be made] within a town or in the open country<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_24.robnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="465" ed="#whitelock"/>And no one is to buy anything worth more than fourpence, neither live-stock nor other goods, unless he has the trustworthy witness of four men, whether it is in the borough or in the country.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="267" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And no one shall buy anything worth more than four pence, either livestock or goods, unless he has four men as honest witnesses, whether he is in a town or in the country.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="326"><ref target="clause:IVEg_6-2">IV Eg 6.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. IV Eg. 6, 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_24-2">II Cn 24.2</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_45">Leis Wl 45</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘peniwurð’ is so at a line end, perhaps forgetting ‘-ga’ at the start of the next line. Liebermann compares IV Eg 6.2.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 327, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">24—28 <hi rend="italic">Anfang fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">24—beginning of 28 lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">bebycge, <hi rend="italic">aber</hi> be <hi rend="italic">radirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">bebycge, but be erased</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. in</hi> upp</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered in the 16th cent. to upp</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">falsch;</hi> ne mort ne vif <hi rend="italic">richtig Leis Wil.</hi> 45</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">incorrect; ne mort ne vif correctly in Leis Wil. 45</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ciuitatem <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ciuitatem added by Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðinge ne gebicge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðinge ne gebicge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">penigweorþe <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> i <hi rend="italic">endet Zeile, vielleicht vergass zu Anfang der folgenden</hi> -ga <hi rend="italic">G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">penigweorþe Ld; i ends the line; perhaps G forgot -ga at the beginning of the next</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">getreowe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">getreowe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">up <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">up Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rios <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rios Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rem <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Cb</hi> [n. m. <hi rend="italic">richtige Erklärung zu</hi> n. i.]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rem added by Cb [n. m. correct explanation of n. i.]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.oe.10-3" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Übersetzt durch Leis Wl 45. [Streiche ² letzter Zeile]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Translated by Leis Wl 45. [Delete ² in the last line]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D. i. 1 Merc. Schilling. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kaufzeugen 6; Handel 8b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">I.e. 1 Merc. shilling. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kaufzeugen 6; Handel 8b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.de1.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">todte Fahrhabe</hi>³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">inanimate movable goods</hi>³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_24.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht etwa ‘Grundeigen’, vielmehr ‘dead stock’ Plummer (<hi rend="italic">Saxon chron</hi>. II 115), andere Beispiele Toller 637 I Ende. Unter <hi rend="italic">immobile</hi> (vielleicht auch <hi rend="italic">iacens</hi> Inst) versteht Hn 59, 21 (d. i. Verf. von Q) ebenfalls kleine tote Werte im Ggs. zu Vieh</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not, say, ‘landed property’, but rather ‘dead stock’ Plummer (<hi rend="italic">Saxon chron</hi>. II 115); other examples Toller 637 I end. By <hi rend="italic">immobile</hi> (perhaps also <hi rend="italic">iacens</hi> Inst) Hn 59, 21 (i.e. the author of Q) likewise understands small inanimate valuables in contrast to livestock</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_24.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann, following Inst. (<hi rend="italic">rem mortuam vel iacentem</hi>) and Cons. (<hi rend="italic">quicquam tam vivum quam mortuum</hi>), explains <hi rend="italic">licgende</hi> as ‘todte Fahrhabe,’ <hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> dead stock, see Plummer, <hi rend="italic">Sax. Chr.</hi> <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>. p. 115, BT. p. 637, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi> <hi rend="italic">licgan</hi>, <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. (end), where other examples of the use of the term are quoted. Q renders the phrase <hi rend="italic">mobile vel immobile</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_24.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. In. 25; Af. 34; I Edw. 1; II As. 12; 13, 1; IV As. 2; VI, 10; IV Edg. 6.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_24.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><label>up</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">In 16th cent. changed to <hi rend="italic">upp</hi> in B.</seg></note>
      </div>
